  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The heights, in centimetres, of 10 players on a basketball team are shown.\n\n170, 180, 185, 188, 192, 193, 193, 194, 196, 202\n\nIs the height of the shortest player on the team considered an outlier? Justify your answer with calculations.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. $170\\text{ cm}<171.5\\text{ cm}$, the lower fence.",
      "worked": "$Q_1=185\\text{ cm}$ and $Q_3=194\\text{ cm}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{IQR}&=Q_3-Q_1\\\\\\text{IQR}&=194-185\\\\\\text{IQR}&=9\\text{ cm}\\\\\\text{Lower fence}&=Q_1-1.5\\times\\text{IQR}\\\\\\text{Lower fence}&=185-1.5\\times9\\\\\\text{Lower fence}&=171.5\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $170<171.5$, the shortest player's height is an outlier.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 47
  },
